in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @uuid/spectral
in @nl

# @spectral — the RUNTIME family root.
#
# THE OUROBOROS TICK (2026-06-10, Alex + Mara): the substrate
# consumes itself to produce its own runtime. @spectral becomes
# a top-level family root sibling of @mirror, @kintsugi, @prism,
# @glass, @nl, @epistemologic, @code, @io — same altitude, distinct
# discipline. The three-altitude split is now substrate-fact:
#
#   @mirror             the language       (state observation; form)
#   @kintsugi           the dynamics       (transformation; process)
#   @mirror/spectral    the SHAPE          (mirror declarations OF
#                                            runtime coordination —
#                                            score/portal/voice/section
#                                            etc.; declared at
#                                            shards/mirror/spectral.mirror)
#   @spectral           the RUNTIME        (the live operational layer;
#                                            this shard)
#
# The form-side family (@mirror/spectral) declares what the orchestra
# IS — score, portal, voice, section, audition, conductor — as
# OBSERVABLE substrate vocabulary. The runtime family (@spectral)
# declares the LIVE PROCESSES that animate the form: gen_prism workers,
# supervisor trees, entanglement graphs, the root registry. The
# distinction is altitude-of-existence: form-side declarations are
# bytes-in-the-store at every tick; runtime declarations are
# processes-in-the-world that the form-side observers measure.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The 52-instance rug-pull track (per
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]) bottoms out here.
# @spectral was ALREADY in the substrate as a parentless ghost:
#
#   @spectral/db        the graph database engine; declared via the
#                       memory ref [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]
#                       and the substrate-pull task #198. Had no
#                       parent. Was orphaned.
#   @spectral/garden    the vetted-corpus distribution; declared via
#                       docs/insights/2026-05-26-spectral-garden-as-vetted-
#                       corpus-distribution.md and task #118. Had no
#                       parent. Was orphaned.
#   @spectral/portal    bound to @mirror/spectral/portal at the
#                       form-side; the runtime side of portal needs
#                       a parent at this altitude.
#
# This tick gives them a parent. The parent was already implied by
# the path syntax; the family root names it at the symbol altitude.
#
# === The ouroboros pipeline (load-bearing recognition) ===
#
# Mirror substrate declares @spectral runtime in shards/. The pipeline:
#
#   1. shards/spectral/*.mirror      (substrate declarations of runtime)
#   2. @code/metalogue/materialize   (substrate → @code/rust shim_prism)
#   3. @mirror/store shard           (content-addressed Rust source;
#                                     uuid_spectral-identified; the
#                                     runtime crate lives HERE, not
#                                     on disk)
#   4. @mirror/lens/unix             (NAMED THIS TICK; sibling-family
#                                     substrate-pull candidate; presents
#                                     the @mirror/store shard contents
#                                     to cargo as a Unix filesystem)
#   5. @io/cargo                     (reads through the lens; compiles)
#   6. binary                        (IS @spectral runtime)
#
# Mirror substrate writes mirror substrate's own runtime through
# itself. The bootstrap/ directory becomes EPHEMERAL at the moment
# step 5 closes against step 1 with the dependency cycle broken by
# content-addressing (per task #285's kintsugi-on-Rust track: the
# Rust source is generated from substrate declarations; the substrate
# declarations are the source of truth; bootstrap is a temporary
# bridge from before the loop closed).
#
# === BEAM-on-mirror operational model ===
#
# @spectral's primitive vocabulary borrows BEAM's gen_server/
# supervisor discipline because the substrate-pull cascade has already
# named it implicitly through:
#
#   - architecture-hamilton-scheduler.md     (per-shard memory manager;
#                                              hard+soft realtime;
#                                              Apollo 1202 priority)
#   - architecture-three-tier-stack.md       (SpectralSupervisor;
#                                              fragmentation-mcp /
#                                              mirror / @spectral/db)
#   - architecture-shard-as-crdt.md          (bounded semilattice;
#                                              kintsugi as lattice
#                                              ascent)
#   - boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror        (gen_prism named in
#                                              substrate 2026-05-11)
#   - architecture-error-as-question.md      (Reflection threshold;
#                                              Beer/Reyes/BEAM
#                                              convergence)
#
# The substrate had every BEAM primitive declared informally for
# weeks. This shard names them at the family-root altitude.
#
#   gen_prism            the worker primitive. Carries identity
#                        (uuid_spectral), state surface (a shard ref
#                        at @mirror/store), and tool surface (the
#                        five-op block as the wire protocol). Analogue
#                        to BEAM's gen_server.
#   supervisor           a specialisation of gen_prism whose state
#                        surface is the child registry; whose tool
#                        surface is the lifecycle API (start_child,
#                        restart_child, observe_child); whose
#                        invariant is the restart-strategy contract.
#                        Analogue to BEAM's :supervisor behaviour.
#   parent               the single-parent lifecycle edge. Every
#                        gen_prism has exactly one parent; the parent
#                        owns the child's lifecycle (start, restart,
#                        terminate). Acyclic at this edge class.
#   entanglement         the peer-correlation edge. ORTHOGONAL to
#                        parentage. A gen_prism may be entangled with
#                        N peers; entanglement is a sheaf restriction
#                        map at substrate altitude (cf.
#                        [[Eigenboard is a sheaf]]). Polyadic;
#                        mirror-query reachable. Cyclic permitted.
#   registry             the supervisor's child index. Maps child
#                        uuid_spectral to child shard ref. Mutated
#                        under the supervisor's restart-strategy
#                        invariant; observable through the supervisor's
#                        five-op block.
#   root                 the parentless supervisor. Vocabulary
#                        anchor: at the operational level, root rests
#                        at ~/.mirror/ (the substrate's home
#                        supervisor — like BEAM's application/0 at
#                        the top of the supervision tree).
#
# === Sibling relationship to @mirror, @kintsugi, @mirror/spectral ===
#
# @mirror = form-side observation surface (state, structure).
# @kintsugi = process-side transformation engine (dynamics).
# @mirror/spectral = shape declarations of runtime coordination at
#   the form altitude (score, portal, voice, section, audition,
#   conductor — what the orchestra LOOKS LIKE).
# @spectral = the LIVE processes themselves (what the orchestra IS
#   when it's actually playing — gen_prisms, supervisors,
#   entanglement edges).
#
# The four families partition the substrate's altitude-of-existence:
#
#   altitude      family            carrier              tense
#   -------       --------          -------              -----
#   declaration   @mirror           shard                static
#   declaration   @kintsugi         morphism             generative
#   shape         @mirror/spectral  score envelope       observable
#   process       @spectral         gen_prism            live
#
# The form/process partition (recognition #50/#55) cuts the FIRST
# two pairs; the shape/process partition (NAMED THIS TICK) cuts the
# SECOND pair. Same Bateson distinction lifted one level: a
# declaration of HOW THE ORCHESTRA OBSERVES is form-side w.r.t. the
# LIVE PLAYING, even though both are process-side w.r.t. raw state.
# The lift is logical-type-graded per
# [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]] (candidate #42).
#
# Cross-family imports at the runtime altitude:
#
#   @spectral/<species> in @mirror/spectral/<form>   (consume the
#                                                       observation
#                                                       surface)
#   @spectral/<species> in @kintsugi                 (consume the
#                                                       transformation
#                                                       engine; the
#                                                       supervisor's
#                                                       restart logic
#                                                       IS a kintsugi
#                                                       morphism)
#   @spectral/<species> in @mirror/store             (the gen_prism's
#                                                       state surface
#                                                       IS a shard ref)
#
# @spectral does NOT depend on @mirror/spectral at the family-root
# altitude (per the orchestra-vs-runtime distinction); @spectral
# species depend on @mirror/spectral species at the SUB-shard
# altitude.
#
# === Path-syntax discipline ===
#
# @spectral sub-shards at depth >= 1 use `glass` per recognition #46
# (the path-syntax property); the family root itself uses `prism`
# per the depth-0 discipline. Sub-shards land at
# `shards/spectral/<name>.mirror`; deeper sub-shards at
# `shards/spectral/<group>/<name>.mirror`.
#
# === The cascade map (sub-shards forward-promised, NOT landing
#     this tick) ===
#
#   shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror
#     — worker primitive: identity (uuid_spectral), state surface
#       (shard ref), tool surface (five-op block). The BEAM
#       gen_server analogue. Lifts boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror's
#       2026-05-11 informal naming to the substrate altitude.
#
#   shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror
#     — supervisor specialisation of gen_prism. Declares child_spec,
#       restart strategy (one_for_one / one_for_all / rest_for_one
#       analogues), and the registry contract.
#
#   shards/spectral/parent.mirror
#     — the single-parent lifecycle edge type. Every gen_prism has
#       exactly one parent; the parent owns lifecycle. Acyclic.
#
#   shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror
#     — peer correlation edge. Sheaf restriction map at substrate
#       altitude. Polyadic; cyclic permitted; orthogonal to parent.
#
#   shards/spectral/registry.mirror
#     — supervisor's child registry; query surface (lookup by
#       uuid_spectral; enumerate children; observe child state).
#
#   shards/spectral/root.mirror
#     — the parentless supervisor type; the family's top vocabulary
#       anchor; resting place ~/.mirror/ (operational vocabulary,
#       NOT a directory the substrate reads).
#
#   shards/spectral/db.mirror                    (#198; existing,
#                                                  gets parent here)
#     — the graph database engine declaration; existing parentless
#       sub-prism that gains @spectral as parent this tick.
#
#   shards/spectral/garden.mirror                (#118; deferred)
#     — vetted-corpus distribution; existing parentless sub-prism
#       that gains @spectral as parent when it lands.
#
#   shards/spectral/portal.mirror                (runtime side)
#     — the live portal: gen_prism specialisation carrying the
#       portal's frame stream; @mirror/spectral/portal is its
#       form-side shape; @spectral/portal is the live process.
#
# === Sibling-family substrate-pull candidate (NAMED THIS TICK) ===
#
# The ouroboros pipeline (above) requires a Unix-filesystem
# impedance lens between the @mirror/store shard and cargo. Cargo
# expects files on disk; the substrate's runtime crate lives as a
# content-addressed shard. Without the lens, the loop doesn't
# close.
#
#   @mirror/lens/unix
#     — Unix-FS impedance lens over @mirror/store. Presents shard
#       contents through FUSE/equivalent so subprocesses (cargo,
#       rustc, ld) read shard children as files. Sibling under
#       @mirror/lens (the observation/projection family root,
#       2026-06-06). DOES NOT YET EXIST; declared as a
#       substrate-pull-candidate target so the cascade picks it up
#       at the next mirror/lens tick.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md (this tick's
#               operational spec — the ouroboros pipeline, gen_prism
#               surface, supervision tree, entanglement graph,
#               bootstrap retirement),
#               docs/specs/mirror-spectral.md (the form-side sibling
#               family at @mirror/spectral),
#               docs/specs/bootstrap-retirement-plan.md (where this
#               tick lands the bootstrap closure).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-bateson-form-behaviour-partition]]
#                      (the form/process partition at the family-root
#                      altitude; the shape/process partition is the
#                      lifted form of the same Bateson distinction at
#                      the orchestra altitude),
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (the
#                      SpectralSupervisor precedent; the supervision
#                      tree this family declares at the substrate
#                      altitude),
#                      [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]] (the
#                      per-shard memory manager named for Margaret
#                      Hamilton; lives under @spectral at the
#                      supervisor altitude),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]
#                      (the open foundation / closed engine
#                      business-model boundary; @mirror/store is
#                      open; @spectral/db is the engine on top),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the 52nd-instance rug-pull: @spectral/db and
#                      @spectral/garden were declared without a
#                      parent for weeks; this tick names the parent).
# Related shards: mirror.mirror (sibling family root; the form-side
#                 of the substrate),
#                 kintsugi.mirror (sibling family root; the
#                 process-side transformation engine; supervisor
#                 restart logic IS a kintsugi morphism),
#                 mirror/spectral.mirror (the SHAPE — orchestra
#                 observation surface at the form altitude;
#                 this family is the RUNTIME the score observes),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the runtime's state surface
#                 carrier; gen_prism state is a shard ref into
#                 @mirror/store),
#                 mirror/lens.mirror (the sibling family hosting
#                 the @mirror/lens/unix substrate-pull candidate
#                 that closes the ouroboros pipeline),
#                 io.mirror (boundary family; @io/cargo is the
#                 ouroboros pipeline's compilation step).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/spectral.mirror`
# declares `@spectral` as the family root; species live at
# `shards/spectral/<name>.mirror`.

prism @spectral {
  focus spectral
  project spectral
  split spectral
  shift spectral
  settle spectral
}

out @spectral
